165x|a|Worthy of belief; probable; credible; as, a likely story. ; Having probability; having or giving reason to expect; -- followed by the infinitive; as, it is likely to rain. ; Similar; like; alike. ; Such as suits; good-looking; pleasing; agreeable; handsome. ; Having such qualities as make success probable; well adapted to the place; promising; as, a likely young man; a likely servant.	j:h4q,43,4;29n7,28,8;27f2,22,4;1dr8,21,2;1lwy,21,2;jfy,16,2;293z,16,2;1o99,14,6;1eun,12,8;12n7,10,4~29n7,28,8;1eun,12,8;1o99,14,6;12n7,10,4;1kic,3,4;h4q,43,4;psw,6,4;27f2,22,4;1kib,8,4;za8,5,3	e:1xkf,23,5;p3e,3,6~p3e,3,6;1xkf,23,5
