16g8|n|The art or process of putting designs or writing, with a greasy material, on stone, and of producing printed impressions therefrom. The process depends, in the main, upon the antipathy between grease and water, which prevents a printing ink containing oil from adhering to wetted parts of the stone not covered by the design. See Lithographic limestone, under Lithographic.	n:1dsg,114,2~1dsg,114,2
16hq|n|The act or process of litigating; a suit at law; a judicial contest.	a:cxu,96,4~cxu,96,4	N:qdb,43,3~qdb,43,3
16hv|n|A dyestuff extracted from certain lichens (Roccella tinctoria, Lecanora tartarea, etc.), as a blue amorphous mass which consists of a compound of the alkaline carbonates with certain coloring matters related to orcin and orcein.	a:vdr,38,7~vdr,38,7	N:21hb,66,5~21hb,66,5
